 # Flowmaster Validate
 
-FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION: 3.2.10
+FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION: 3.2.12
 
 Maintenance addition: register the self-contained human-design-reading-flowmaster domain
 contract without changing the Primary core or existing domain/oracle checks. Its behavioral
@@ -35,6 +35,38 @@
 moves with it; validation behaviour changes again, so `FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION` is
 incremented to 3.2.10. Both skills ship together and install together.
 
+Round 24 carries two corrections and changes no prompt body and no contract. `F1`, raised by
+the independent §10 review of round 23 and accepted without argument: round 23 shipped
+`SF10-09`'s validation behaviour while still emitting `validator_revision: 3.2.8`, the
+identity round 22's report on `main` already records measurements against from different
+bytes. The counts coincided and that coincidence was the hazard, so `validator_revision`
+moves to **3.2.9** at its four sites. Because 3.2.10 is installed and bound to a published
+§10 verdict, corrected bytes must not reuse it, so `FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION` moves to
+**3.2.11** in the same change. `SF10-11` closes a coverage gap `D5` concealed: the class-map
+fixture renamed in round 21 tests a *retargeted* CRD destination, and nothing exercised an
+*absent* CRD branch. Two fixtures are added, and falsification decides which: dropping the
+mapping half of `len(rows) != 2 or mapping != expected` leaves only
+`reject-source-epic-to-crd` failing, and dropping the length half leaves only
+`reject-source-duplicate-crd-class-branch` failing. Each half of the guard now has a case
+that uniquely fires it; before this round the length half had none. `change-flow` is untouched and stays at 3.2.8; only this skill's bytes
+move, so only this skill needs a fresh §10.
+
+Round 25 answers the limit the independent review of round 24 exposed, and carries that review's
+one finding. `SF10-12`: the validator computed `prompt_body_sha256`, reported it, and **compared it
+with nothing**, so a rebuilt corpus could be verified by nobody but the session that built it --
+which is why the reviewer correctly declined to run the 55-body gate and reported the limit rather
+than a number. The 55 body identities were already recorded, in the approved registry's
+`evidence_contract`; they were simply never checked. They are now pinned in the validation profile
+and compared on every run, with exactly one trailing newline stripped first, because the pin is a
+property of the Notion page and not of the file that holds it. Missing pins are an error, not a
+silent skip. The round also corrects the round-24 comment that said the absence fixture "isolates
+the arity branch" -- it does not, as that round's own falsification showed -- and that said row
+deletion trips `PROMPT_HANDOFF_RECEIVER` here, which is true of the end-to-end validator and not of
+the checker the fixture calls. Validation behaviour changes, so `validator_revision` moves to
+**3.2.10** at its four sites and `FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION` to **3.2.12**: 3.2.9 and 3.2.11 are
+bound to the published §10 verdict naming `e8f30b9a...`, and corrected bytes must not reuse an
+identity a verdict already describes. `change-flow` is untouched and stays at 3.2.8.
+
